# tools/m/medial_axis_witness.rish -- a shape's metric spine, the ridge of the distance field, proves itself on metal (Season G).
#
# Season G (Open Media Primitives) -- the natural consumer of image/distance.rye. The distance rung gives every foreground pixel
# its depth to the nearest background pixel; the LOCAL MAXIMA of that field trace the shape's spine. This rung reads that crest --
# the medial axis by the distance route, the complement of image/zhang_suen.rye's thinning: the ridge remembers the thickness
# where thinning guarantees unit width.
#
# The crux this witness proves on metal: a solid 3x3 block reads depth 6 at its center and 3 around its ring, so the medial axis
# is that single center spine pixel -- the SAME point Zhang-Suen thins the block to, reached by the metric ridge not by peeling
# boundary points; a one-pixel line reads uniform depth 3 so the ridge keeps it whole; a 2-tall strip reads depth 3 across both
# rows so the ridge comes back two pixels wide (the distance medial axis is honestly NOT unit-width); a lone dot is its own spine;
# colorize renders the medial axis transform (the spine alone ramped by depth) round-tripping through the open QOI codec
# byte-for-byte; an empty field refuses by name. No network, no key, no funds -- the spine a surface reads the day it asks where
# the middle of a mark runs.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/m/medial_axis_witness.rish

say "medial_axis: Language EN -- Season G metric spine; the ridge of local maxima of the chamfer distance field, the medial axis by the distance route."
say "medial_axis: Style Radiant -- compose not braid: this rung owns only the local-maximum ridge test and the two renders; distance owns the field, branch.is_on reads a mask back through the one shared door, qoi owns the buffer, color.mix ramps the depth."
say "medial_axis: Lens TAME -- the ridge buffer is bounded by the field's pixel count; an off-image neighbor is ground never a phantom; an empty field refuses by name up front so a refusal allocates nothing; no network, no key, no funds."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "image/bin/medial_axis"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p image/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build image/medial_axis.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "medial_axis: build failed -- ${build.err}"

let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "medial_axis: selftest exited non-zero -- ${selftest.out}"

let out = trim selftest.out
say "medial_axis: ${out}"

assert selftest.out contains "GREEN image-medial_axis" else "medial_axis: selftest did not print the GREEN line"

say "medial_axis: GREEN -- the ridge of the distance field is a shape's metric spine (the block's single center, the line kept whole, the 2-wide strip honestly two pixels thick), colorize renders the medial axis transform round-tripping through the open QOI codec, on metal."
